{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>If he be your prophet, HaShem.</b> Like (II Chronicles 15:8) והנבואה עודד הנביא. Its sense is: if he be your prophet, a prophet of HaShem. And He says: whoever among you is a prophet, even if he is a prophet of HaShem, he does not prophesy by His great Name but only in a vision (mar'eh) or in riddles; and He mentioned this because many of the prophets do not attain to this. But 'your prophet' means through the holy spirit (ru'ach ha-kodesh), in the manner of what is said (II Samuel 23:2): ״רוח HaShem דבר בי״, which is the 'hand of HaShem' spoken of in Ezekiel. And the reason He said במראה אליו אתודע — 'I make Myself known to him in a vision' — and did not say במראה אליו אראה — 'I appear to him in a vision' — this verse is like the verse (Exodus 6:3): וארא אל אברהם אל יצחק ואל יעקב באל שדי ושמי HaShem לא נודעתי להם. He says that the great Name HaShem will be in a vision, and through it He makes Himself known to the prophet — not by His great Name, as He said, ושמי HaShem לא נודעתי להם. And He said that speech will be in a dream; but not so My servant Moses, for בכל ביתי נאמן הוא — in the house through which the prophets see dreams, he is faithful; and he knows all the attributes himself, and speech from mouth to mouth will be his from Me, and the form he beholds, he does not see it in a dream. And here He taught what distinguishes the prophecy of Moses from that of the other prophets." "<b>I make Myself known to him in a vision.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): in night visions, and this is what He said: בחלום אדבר." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: במראה ('in a vision') is the vision of the sefirot called Nezah and Hod, and it is called Tzeva'ot as well, for to that point the prophecy of all the prophets reaches. For when they enter through the first gate and the portal designated for prophets to enter, their prophecy ascends and reaches that place and no further. And the sign for this is (Exodus 38:8): במראות הצובאות אשר צבאו פתח אהל מועד — and from there they ascend and prophesy through the mirrors of the hosts (be-mar'ot ha-tzov'ot)." "<b>And it is fitting</b> that you contemplate how, when He encompassed here all the degrees of prophecy — both that of Moses our master, peace be upon him, and that of the other prophets — He used for the other prophets the term מראה with a qamatz, which is a word indicating imaginings and the confusion of prophecy." "<b>And what appears</b> to be the reason for the matter: He wished to compare the prophecy of the other prophets to one who gazes into a mirror (mar'ah), and this is the language of our Rabbis of blessed memory: 'One may not look in a mirror on the Sabbath' — meaning a glass mirror, in which the one gazing sees the image of his form from within it by the power of the mirror's polishing, but there is nothing inside it. So too the prophecy of the other prophets: because they behold those holy, pure forms and the supernal luminaries from within the brilliance and brightness of those mighty lights, there appear to them imaginings, and they see there a form like the form of a man, as it is written (Hosea 12:11): וביד הנביאים אדמה. But Moses our master, peace be upon him — since his prophecy was superior to all of theirs — saw nothing of those imaginings at all, but rather a true vision close to the intellect. And therefore through the clarity of his prophecy it was known and recognized that there is no likeness or form there at all, only His glory. This is what is written: ותמונת HaShem יביט — He attributed the form to Him, not that He has a form, heaven forbid; and likewise (Genesis 1:27): בצלם אלהים — not that He has an image or likeness, heaven forbid. And this is what our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded: 'All the prophets, all of them, gazed through a speculum that does not shine,' and they brought a proof from Ezekiel, in whom is written many visions (Ezekiel 1:1): ואראה מראות אלהים, (ibid.): ואראה כעין חשמל, and many imaginings. But Moses, peace be upon him, gazed through the speculum that shines, as it is said: ומראה ולא בחידות."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:02.567050095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}